  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Promenade Hei is a surface colony on the Berg's northern reach, established during the Frozen Peace by settlers led by Grand Auditor Mingmeyang under the governance of the Qingqe'frostlings, a faction within Aurora Stack's administrative hierarchy. Once a prosperous trade settlement distinguished by its crystal spires and open-air merchant galleries, the colony retains its official designation as thriving. The ice does not support this classification.
    
    ## Founding and Early Development
    
    The Aerie Perch — the colony's first permanent structure, now locally called "The Watching" for reasons residents decline to specify — was raised by Mingmeyang's original settlers and remains operational as a crystal-working and trade facility. The colony grew around it, terraced into the berg in the old vertical style, with the spires serving as both aurora-light collectors and navigational markers. Mingmeyang herself remains resident, though accounts from the chroniclers describe her as deteriorating — "beloved and slowly hollow" is the phrase that recurs.
    
    The colony's early survival owed something to the beacon-keeper Lianhinglou, who entered forbidden deep chambers to recover ancient techniques for mapping krill blooms during a resource collapse. The Shell Hatch method Lianhinglou taught Mingmeyang extended the colony's supplies at the cost of Lianhinglou's memories and left both practitioners bearing crystalline scarring. Whether the corruption now afflicting the colony traces to these early compromises is disputed. I note only that the timeline is suggestive.
    
    ## The Darkening and Corruption
    
    The Darkening — a seventeen-day failure of aurora-light through the colony's spires — collapsed trade and marked the onset of visible corruption. This manifests as cold-burn discoloration in the ice and a whispering residents describe, with studied vagueness, as *conversational*. Corruption has reached the mid-terraces. Fourteen residents are classified as Touched — functional but altered, speaking to presences others cannot perceive. The Qingqe'frostlings reclassified them as a protected labor category and assigned them to the lower terraces, where corruption was worst and no one else would serve. Corrupt amber-tinged aurora-crystals have appeared in shipments originating from the adjacent Aerie Perch.
    
    During the Long Dark, the boundary thinned sufficiently that transparent ancestors walked the Promenade visible to all.
    
    ## Current Conditions
    
    | Terrace Level | Population | Status |
    |---|---|---|
    | Upper terraces | 412 | Strained but functional |
    | Lower terraces | 91 | Corruption-affected; staffed primarily by Touched |
    
    Fire-core shipments from the Nightshelf arrive consistently below requisite amounts, the shortfall widening as each party interprets different amendments of the Long-dark Edict against different baselines. The chronicle of the Forty-Eighth Amendment documents the resulting administrative spiral: each bureaucratic correction generating new contradictions, rationing formulas incentivizing migration toward corrupted zones, cleansing protocols requiring resources the colony does not possess.
    
    Someone has carved initials into the Orca Incursion memorial wall. They match no name listed above them. No one has explained this either.
